{"title":"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(No_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (No bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/33901614db4565ea5dfabf01b3c25e3c9673e97e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC.$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> A circle which is internally tangent with the circumscribed circle of the triangle is also tangent to the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547f225d9af24dda08195ad51ee009872c3d3fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> in the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede78a06018011f48c24a76284afce482ebc6c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> respectively <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b727b773d199f4fa0d684957a720f9c3e9750c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> Prove that the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is the center of the inscribed circle of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd222166def59a3315433877917a826de6488031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28No_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(No_bash)\">Solution 1 (No bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (No bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the mentioned circle internally tangent to the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let the midpoint of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> be denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and let the midpoint of arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is the diameter of the circumcircle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1f2c80f1cad2cdbe6d0ed229c901dec289d5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABM = 90 \\deg$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35b19db53c4382abe9bff4f53565c9c5eaad2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP \\perp AB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> by tangency, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcc9ecb8e7c6fb80766c186721353e6c3dc398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8068607716f3c2549af1dc978d77a422ca7201dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. Then \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/febe4b1aa705d6503b7682d7521a86a9f29da2cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\angle PMN = \\angle PMQ = \\frac{1}{2} \\angle POQ = \\angle PON = \\angle BMN\\]\" width=\"420\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d1675631bef871d4c7e508c7550e72be9b8c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BMP = \\angle PMN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"151\" height=\"14\" />. Triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47afcd0c4abdafbd91d3b2ea5237279cf19cd5cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PNM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/5163f6755a664731c9d1d30c0119fb751a9b2186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBM$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> must be congruent, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b376105175cf6acf0915ae806afe228e790cc6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" />. Now, it is a fact that the incenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87b672a08b6fc66442fc41ccb805c991a2ac1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI=IM=IC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" /> (from say angle chasing), and clearly, there is only one point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> inside the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08da4b52d8ec86c605b7210f8dd6c47b023914d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=BX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/a/c3af336fcc5d9d38a30afb0f5b1523740b61c692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=X=I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001\" title=\"Ddk001\">Ddk001</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c10514951db2865d95a7f389c98b9917a08e77d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = BC, b = AB = AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" /> the triangle sides, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bbb8f7ed83f8eae1b8744b9437918932811e22f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r, R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> the triangle inradius and circumradius and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009cf3eeb0ff3789cc057632947cadb200ab4663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> the triangle semiperimeter and area. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/9775f30fee24ec664151f56fe63ce8349fa8aba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S, T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> be the tangency points of the incircle (I) with the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547f225d9af24dda08195ad51ee009872c3d3fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/8574f36470fbc7b0993b3173981a8cf08b597bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K, L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> be the midpoints of of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5cbb73e32f7cb3c1c850a652282b69085268e78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> the midpoint of the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> of the circumcircle (O) opposite to the vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The isosceles triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04dc970ead0037a0e5a5938a6a43bb37d7a7a2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AST \\sim \\triangle APQ \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"220\" height=\"17\" /> are all centrally similar with the homothety center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. The homothety coefficient for the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73947830921dd98ca6627d15cf5e5ca666508c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AST \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc38b04087b369e992c2926e613aa9b44e4b59a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{13} = \\frac{AS}{AB} = \\frac{s - a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" />. The homothety coefficient for the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d254505da9b3949f77cfdccbb0d5cdad01e30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AST \\sim \\triangle APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e8a9cf5e80ec0a03dba58c3e71edfc2c739a855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{12} = \\frac{AS}{AP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. The point K is the tangency point of the incircle (I) with the side BC, while the point M is the tangency point of the given circle with the triangle circumcircle (O). It follows that the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b75a517bec4103d3b98033c2ea3b7b309562c209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ASK \\sim \\triangle APM$\" width=\"146\" height=\"13\" /> are also centrally similar with the homothety center A and the same homothety coefficient as the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d254505da9b3949f77cfdccbb0d5cdad01e30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AST \\sim \\triangle APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/d/c2dbf582cf671ffff39d079db220c21f52fa127f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{12} = \\frac{AS}{AP} = \\frac{AK}{AM} = \\frac{h}{2R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"192\" height=\"38\" />, where h = AK is the A-altitude of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. The homothety coefficient of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526d142a5d571a73be3458d7baa985b1ff26f785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APQ \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322678493ab59b923b7d6b8e8269922ca2aac1c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{23} = \\frac{h_{12}}{h_{13}} = \\frac{s - a}{b} \\cdot \\frac{2R}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"184\" height=\"40\" /> Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a728603b77a978cb3bb613da9157f3d57003f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h&#39; = AL$\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />-altitude of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89cb1776431d56dcf6668eaeed7e634677d3215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />. Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb17c322f90e642dfa7270d6e89b06193c326051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h&#39;}{h} = h_{23} = \\frac{s - a}{b} \\cdot \\frac{2R}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b308293f6a810bb398287bf739a234dc4120b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = h - h&#39; = h - 2R\\ \\frac{s - a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"229\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/789be997e8a5b83eadb6151833eac09d05fa36ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\frac{2 \\triangle}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb05b12e58ba9bc1ad7fe8b2576c4e6c02578f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2R = \\frac{ab^2}{2 \\triangle}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a6ccff902b9e07a900f4cf4dbb940720c5b374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s - a = \\frac{\\triangle^2}{s(s - b)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"135\" height=\"43\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38df2ab7f542a05515d43682fdcbe7c4ec09d812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = \\frac{2 \\triangle}{a} - \\frac{ab^2}{2 \\triangle} \\cdot \\frac{\\triangle^2}{bs(s - b)^2} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"246\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>(substituting 2s = 2b + a and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e4889519da08b7425c6b4f8e896369d7f3678cba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s - b = \\frac a 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"33\" /> for an isosceles triangle)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b805c7ddcce770a9bcd8deaf2ac52c34bc64b26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{\\triangle}{s}\\left(\\frac{2s}{a} - \\frac{ab}{2(s - b)^2}\\right) = \\frac{\\triangle}{s} \\left(\\frac{2b}{a} + 1 - \\frac{2b}{a}\\right) = \\frac{\\triangle}{s} = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"431\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>which means that the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c8210720352b98019d8064bc1b3a285f3483a14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L \\equiv I$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> is identical with the incenter of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The above solution was posted and copyrighted by yetti. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p367852\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO\" title=\"1978 IMO\">1978 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172833\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 304/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12543/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.483      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.483      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19715:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172833 and revision id 292910. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}